motivation: Effort is not a mood. It is a hand you extend toward the day.
discipline: The alarm rings. You get up anyway. Tomorrow trusts the small thing you finish today.
money: The money you keep is the money that buys your future freedom.
mindset: Perspective is a slower voice than panic, and it usually tells the truth.
fact: The Eiffel Tower can grow taller in summer as heat expands the iron.
books: We build confidence from what we know and ignore the rare event that changes everything.
stoic: Want what arrives, not what you demanded; the day stops fighting you.
